{% macro streaming_example(slide_id, crossed_out=false) -%}
<section class="slide streaming-jsonld-example" id="{{ slide_id }}">
        <h2>Streaming JSON-LD</h2>
        <p class="example-caption">Read one JSON-LD document → RDF quad events</p>
        <pre class="code-example"><code class="hljs" id="{{ slide_id }}-code" data-source="examples/read-jsonld.mjs"></code></pre>
        <p class="example-caption implementation-links"><a href="https://github.com/rubensworks/jsonld-streaming-parser.js"><img class="github-mark" src="github-mark.svg" alt="GitHub"> rubensworks/jsonld-streaming-parser.js</a> · <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11-streaming/">Specification</a></p>
        <aside>
            <p>The <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11-streaming/">Note</a>
                was published on 7 May 2020. Required key ordering places context
                and type before other properties; early identifiers are recommended.
                It addresses incremental RDF conversion inside one document.</p>
            <p>Implementations include the JavaScript
                <a href="https://github.com/rubensworks/jsonld-streaming-parser.js">parser</a>
                and <a href="https://github.com/rubensworks/jsonld-streaming-serializer.js">serializer</a>,
                plus <a href="https://docs.rs/oxjsonld/latest/oxjsonld/">OxJSON-LD</a>.
                These implementations are existing work; extending this profile is
                outside this CG discussion’s proposed work.</p>
            <p>The visible example uses jsonld-streaming-parser 5.0.2, not a
                standardized JsonLdProcessor streaming method. The input file contains
                one complete JSON-LD document. The async iterator receives RDF/JS
                quads; this example prints its object literal, 20. Its inline
                context avoids fetching a remote context.</p>
            <p>This scope boundary concerns this CG discussion, not the Working Group’s
                charter. Incremental conversion and document sequences can coexist.
                Buffering limitations remain under discussion in
                <a href="https://github.com/w3c/json-ld-streaming/issues/54"><img class="github-mark" src="github-mark.svg" alt="GitHub"> w3c/json-ld-streaming#54</a>
                and <a href="https://github.com/w3c/json-ld-streaming/issues/69"><img class="github-mark" src="github-mark.svg" alt="GitHub"> w3c/json-ld-streaming#69</a>.</p>
        </aside>
        {% if crossed_out %}
        <svg class="scope-cross" viewBox="0 0 1024 576" aria-label="Outside this presentation’s scope" role="img">
            <path d="M 85 65 L 940 510 M 940 65 L 85 510"/>
        </svg>
        {% endif %}
    </section>
{%- endmacro %}
